{"title":"2025 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of ordered triples of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6ee95974a5c111a0e21d3651468fe39f09b7b01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=305$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/b/9bbd10585beedbcad73a127b98ce238d54b4cd78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+bc+ca$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710d09135a91c1c5d11fa4b952d2a3b2fd4d5069.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$305$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebeebeb82324019e785ac4ed1939660d5e758188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\ne 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> is a prime dividing both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/b/9bbd10585beedbcad73a127b98ce238d54b4cd78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+bc+ca$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"14\" />. Consider the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95f266dd4ce8acf99a712bf3a16ddca1bf4682c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = (x-a)(x-b)(x-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"227\" height=\"20\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Expanding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n(x-a)(x-b)(x-c) &amp;\\equiv x^3 - (a+b+c)x^2 + (ab+bc+ca)x - abc \\pmod{p} \\\\\n&amp;\\equiv x^3 - abc \\pmod{p}.\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore, the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> are the cube roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. However, the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> are also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. This gives us two possibilities; either a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> has a triple root at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/aff99c92f43a00c981f676cca13d0f6dc5be0fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\mid p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the three distinct nonzero cube roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f28d9a49b0678bf83a5ec1038d70b2061a0f9508.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\nmid 5-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c01f641bbf145bab8ac586728cbfc447e5373ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\equiv b \\equiv c \\equiv 0 \\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/b/4ab2576746d592c294c70b8a3f6012a3050ba907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c) = (5a_1,5b_1,5c_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"20\" /> for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fc4b9ed6d75d026557e7b06c2ed483c6ed0eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00322295674c54c5413520f7493470ff32ae3cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/64237fb5643cc40b475763ee849edc74d714efb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+b_1+c_1 = 61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/7/937ebfbe00faef33d3f973673bab05ce08970b42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_1,b_1,c_1 &lt; 61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60d4b9bf2ce3517070a2a13e5ddde1862a4f2d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\mid 61-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fc4b9ed6d75d026557e7b06c2ed483c6ed0eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00322295674c54c5413520f7493470ff32ae3cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are the three cube roots of a nonzero cubic residue modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a primitive root modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />; we partition the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfec36121bed8bec23fd7b56959eb015bcd9c1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,\\dots, 60\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> into the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac4b5273cd8be75031c8aa205ab057b8fe9dbe3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_0,S_1,\\dots, S_{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, where for each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee41ce600bc48b127b8f8f0ee1b766009b4ef53d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le j \\le 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebca172452e3b28cd8dd4caf6e4545287afd3ad8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_j \\equiv \\{g^{j}, g^{j+20}, g^{j+40}\\} \\pmod{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"256\" height=\"22\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abdbef5b4af13d3da7469fbdd157e402e04e567f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_1,b_1,c_1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> must be equal to some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2471034924050fbf1b59048c09d74454ea66634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" />. Notice that the element sum of any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2471034924050fbf1b59048c09d74454ea66634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, and for size reasons, the sum must be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a8948c71337e6ef8aac086dd7444c757c379b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$122$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. Recall that we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a4b95960ab013de5ad7ff073339485170994588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+b_1+c_1=61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"17\" />. Hence, we seek the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> such that the element sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2471034924050fbf1b59048c09d74454ea66634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>To do this, we show that there is in fact a bijection between the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2471034924050fbf1b59048c09d74454ea66634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> that have an element sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and those that have one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a8948c71337e6ef8aac086dd7444c757c379b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$122$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a6b6b810cbed90d77d9e9fd35e491b4f644dab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_j = \\{u,v,w\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70bf2dc699a8caf44ce774921e6ed34b87b8b962.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le j \\le 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />, and consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c3d9a7a1ad0ed5eb08053b7aac4e997a9a8811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{j+10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"43\" height=\"19\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1370cbd5256af10860bdbd778662c0460d43d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^{30}\\equiv -1 \\pmod{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" />, we have\n\\begin{align*}\nS_{j+10} &amp;\\equiv \\{g^{j+10},g^{j+30},g^{j+50}\\} \\pmod{61} \\\\\n&amp;\\equiv \\{-g^{j+40}, -g^{j}, -g^{j+20}\\} \\pmod{61} \\\\\n&amp;\\equiv \\{-u,-v,-w\\} \\pmod{61}.\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a2d522236f63baf8e7d00d4b390b347f9c6d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{j+10} = \\{61-u,61-v,61-w\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"257\" height=\"20\" />. The element sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2471034924050fbf1b59048c09d74454ea66634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> plus the element sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c3d9a7a1ad0ed5eb08053b7aac4e997a9a8811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{j+10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"43\" height=\"19\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d0ae020c85a8c5c48aeff0a6b320b766b4278c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$183$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so exactly one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2471034924050fbf1b59048c09d74454ea66634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c3d9a7a1ad0ed5eb08053b7aac4e997a9a8811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{j+10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"43\" height=\"19\" /> has an element sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> while the other has one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a8948c71337e6ef8aac086dd7444c757c379b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$122$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>To finish, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13df5713f4ade0f293c7f61db2774820f475c0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{20}{2}=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"61\" height=\"23\" /> choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abdbef5b4af13d3da7469fbdd157e402e04e567f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_1,b_1,c_1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />, and we can permute the three variables in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3920c5e3f6b2e5749cd75c3853b63ae714d00561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> ways. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/87811ba4d0f3e52569adb4af47331853edebf2db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot 10 = \\boxed{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Sedro\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018032959\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 244/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13646/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33821:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018032959 and revision id 263136. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}